  "question": {
    "text": "Electrons having kinetic energy&nbsp;<math><mn>30</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;are made to collide with atomic hydrogen gas (in ground state) and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>42</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of electron energy is used to excite the hydrogen atoms. The number of emitted wavelengths in emission spectra are"
